=== RitsuLib Auto-Registration Mod Id Mismatch Summary ===
RitsuLib detected assemblies whose ModManager/mod_manifest.json assembly ownership id differs from the ModTypeDiscoveryHub.RegisterModAssembly argument.
This issue only affects RitsuLib auto-discovered types and attributes from those assemblies. Explicit content-pack registrations created with RitsuLibFramework.CreateContentPack or ModContentPackBuilder.For are not affected; attribute-driven pack helpers on auto-discovered types are affected.
Current auto-registration owner/registry ids are resolved from ModManager/mod_manifest.json assembly ownership. This can also determine default public entries for auto-discovered models. A future major RitsuLib release is expected to use the RegisterModAssembly argument as the primary owner id instead.
Mod authors should align their manifest id and runtime mod id, or prepare localization/save compatibility before that update.
If a mod intentionally keeps these ids different, annotate the auto-registration source types with [RitsuLibOwnedBy("...")] to pin those auto-discovered entries to a fixed owner id. For inherited auto-registration attributes, place [RitsuLibOwnedBy("...")] on the type that declares the inherited registration attribute.
Mismatches:
  - assembly='TheQueen', currentAutoRegistrationOwnerId='TheQueen' (source: ModManager/mod_manifest.json assembly ownership), registerModAssemblyArgument='sts2.comicchess.thequeen' (source: ModTypeDiscoveryHub.RegisterModAssembly argument)
